# Advisory

Give `spawns.py` a single DB-facing entry point — `placements(con, harness, session_id) -> list[Placement]` — that owns the child, parent-tool, and message-ordinal queries and then calls the pure `associate_children`, so `session_detail` makes one call instead of assembling four result sets inline. The TDD order and the test list are unchanged; the pure helper still has its own unit tests, and the DB-facing wrapper is covered by the seeded `session_detail` cases already planned.

The payoff is a seam with two more consumers waiting. Spawn-to-turn placement is currently unanswerable in SQL for Cursor (the zip is positional, not a join), so an agent using `sr-query` can see `parent_session_id` but never "which turn launched this subagent, and what was it asked to do." One importable function makes that a future `sr-query` cookbook recipe or `stockroom spawns` subcommand without moving any logic, and it gives QA a non-UI oracle to diff against the `/api/session` payload instead of eyeballing the live dashboard. Cost if declined: `session_detail` grows four more queries inline and the association stays dashboard-private.
